What?"\rI was possessed."\rYour soul is mine!"What's going on?"\rI was under possession.",Entered the purifed and protected zone."&\Pn's Pokémon were fully healed."\r...Give."How? What?"E\rI feel to evil spirits despite my training in the mountains..."B\rCome, child! I have purified this space. You can rest here.Iu;␀�[["\rHahaha."Ha?" \rI feel anemic and weak..."\rReady?"	Huh?"\rWhat's going on here?"\rMy hair is gone.."Say what?"<\rMy hair didn't fall out!\nIt was a malevolent spirit!["\rHahaha."Ha?"-\rIch fühle mich blutarm und schwach..."\rBereit?"	Huh?"\rWas ist hier los?"\rMeine Haare sind weg..."Wie bitte?"I\rMeine Haare sind nicht ausgefallen!\nEs war ein bösartiger Geist!;["\rHahaha."Ha?" \rI feel anemic and weak..."\rReady?"	Huh?"\rWhat's going on here?"\rMy hair is gone.."Say what?"<\rMy hair didn't fall out!\nIt was a malevolent spirit!Iu;␀�[["R\rYou are quite brave for a child. But this will have you running in no time."*\rI'm no longer possessed. Thank you!"8\rOh, you came here so you could challenge Sabrina?" \rThis might help you then."4\rTM121 contains Shadow Punch. It never misses."'\rI wish you luck in your travels.["c\rDu bist ziemlich tapfer für ein Kind. Aber das hier wird dich im Nu in die Flucht schlagen."*\rIch bin nicht mehr besessen. Danke!"?\rOh, du bist hierhergekommen, um Sabrina herauszufordern?"(\rDann könnte dir das hier helfen."F\rTM121 enthält Finsterfaust. Die Attacke schlägt niemals fehl."6\rIch wünsche dir viel Glück auf deinen Reisen.;["R\rYou are quite brave for a child. But this will have you running in no time."*\rI'm no longer possessed. Thank you!"8\rOh, you came here so you could challenge Sabrina?" \rThis might help you then."4\rTM121 contains Shadow Punch. It never misses."'\rI wish you luck in your travels.Iu;␀�[["g\rMisty: You're heading to Celadon City too? It's a beautiful city, full of shops and opportunity."h\rOh, you're going for the gym. I should have guessed as much. Fine, we can have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"No["~\rMisty: Du bist auch auf dem Weg nach Prismania City? Es ist eine wunderschöne Stadt, voller Läden und Möglichkeiten."{\rOh, du willst in die Arena. Das hätte ich mir ja denken können. Na gut, wir können einen Übungskampf bestreiten."1\rMisty: Viel Glück für deinen Arenakampf."\bRasaff"(Möchtest du Rasaff mit dir nehmen?"Ja"	Nein;["g\rMisty: You're heading to Celadon City too? It's a beautiful city, full of shops and opportunity."h\rOh, you're going for the gym. I should have guessed as much. Fine, we can have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"NoIu;␀�_[[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!"[\rLooks like you don't have enough 'mons to battle huh? I'll give you just enough, OK?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\n\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\n\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Sygna Buffs]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."K\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bAlso, about some of their "moves". They're not used by the Pokémon, they're used by the trainer, so they can be used even when the Pokémon's been afflicted with a condition that would normally stop them from moving."�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure, I'll explain them.\nCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages.\nTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses, which provide buffs to their Pokémon."H\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. These are similar to regular moves, except they have a B in front of the move's name. They usually do what the regular move does, with increased power or added effects or the regular effect enhanced.\nPassive Skill - Essentially an ability. How many a Pokémon has here is completely arbitrary."�\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the Pokémon's damage and reduces the damage it takes.\nZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type."Q\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn."]\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika,Giovanni,Red,Red (Thunderbolt), Blue,Leaf]"�\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit. Anyway, his Trainer Move makes his next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but you can protect against it."i\bAlso, don't count on his Tyranitar's Stone Edge to miss. It has better accuracy than you'd expect."�\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move raises her Vaporeon's Defense by 2 stages and all allies' Special Defense by 2 stages."e\bLastly, her Vaporeon's Hydro Pump has a chance to raise its Evasion by 1 stage when it's used."�\bErika's Trainer Move raises her Leafeon's Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage, but if the Sun's up, these stat raises are doubled."\bWith the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled. Lastly, her Leafeon will restore 1/8th of its max HP at the every turn."�\bGiovanni's Nidoking is able to always make its attacks critical hits. Its Mega Kick is a Ground type attack, meaning it gains STAB from it. In addition, Nidoking can also Dynamax and the Max Moves will be critical hits too."�\bRed and his Charizard are insane. His Trainer Move raises Charizard's Attack, Special Attack and Speed by 3 stages and Crit Rate by 2 stages, though its Defense and Special Defense is increased by 1 stage."�\bHis Charizard is also able to use Blast Burn and Solar Beam without needing a (re)charging turn and they will also never miss."\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move maxes out Pikachu's Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since you just throw out 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair."}\bFuthermore, Pikachu's Master Passive, Kanto Flag Bearer, boosts its damage by 10% and reduces its damage taken by 20%."�\bLastly, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a Buddy Move which can be used when Electric Terrain's active. If your Pokémon's paralysed, its Defense and Special Defense are lowered by 1 stage, if they haven't fainted by that point."�\bBlue's Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, it raises the Attack and Special Attack of itself and its allies by 1 stage and heals 1/16th of itself and its allies."p\bAnd then when it attacks, the Defense and Special Defense of itself and its allies are raised by 1 stage."}\bLeaf's Venusaur has a passive skill called Venomous, which badly poisons your Pokémon if your Pokémon is atttacked by it."�\bIn addition to that, the attack will lower the defensive stats of your pokemon, so your pokemon will take even more damage on the next turn. Lastly, Venusaur will heal itself for 1/8th of its health after every attack, because why not?">\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris,Silver]"�\bMorty does a lot. His Trainer Move increases the Defense, Special Defense and Crit Rate of all Pokémon on his side of the field by 1 stage and sets up Tailwind if it isn't already active."�\bEthan's Trainer Move makes the next special attack his Lugia use hit a lot harder than it would, as well as increasing its Accuracy by 1 stage and maxing out its Crit Rate."�\bAlso, his Lugia has a Passive Skill which makes its attacks never miss and Ethan has a Master Passive which boosts its special attacks and reduces damage it takes from opposing special attacks."�\bLyra's Trainer Move increases the Attack and Special Attack of any Pokémon on her side by 2 stages and gives them Gradual Healing."�\bThat's not the crazy thing about this sync pair though. Her Celebi's Grassy Glide makes the opposing Pokémon become confused, trapped AND flinched. Annnnd she can set up Grassy Terrain too."�\bLastly, Lyra has a Master Passive which boosts Celebi's physical attacks (which is just Grassy Glide) as well as reducing the damage it takes from physical attacks."�\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers, because once the Rain is up, her Trainer Move raises all allies' Special Atttack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage, as well as her allies' next special attack doing more damage."�\bApart from that, her Suicune doesn't do much else, though Kris's Master Passive makes it deal a little more damage and reduces the damage it takes from attacks."v\bSilver's Trainer Move increases its Attack and Speed by 3 stages and sets up Tailwind on his side of the field."�\bIn addition, his Sneasel's B Move, B Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. On every hit, the opposing Pokémon's Speed is lowered by 1 stage while its own Evasion and Crit Rate are increased by 1 stage.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move increases the speed of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 2 stages, then increases her Blaziken's Attack by 4 stages and Accuracy by 1 stage and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."K\bBlaziken's Blaze Kick also sharply lowers the Defense of its target."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move increases the Special Attack and Special Defense of all Pokémon on his side of the field by 4 stages as well as increasing their Crit Rate by 1 stage."4\bThen, when his Latios uses Luster Purge, the Special Defense of the target is sharply lowered. But don't think bringing in a Dark type is safe either - when using Draco Meteor his all Pokémon on its side have their Crit Rate increased by 1 stage as well as having their next special attack do more damage."�\bSteven... is a lot, let's just say. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4 forms, each with a Trainer Move."�\bHis first one, "Try This!", sets up Psychic Terrain and raises the user’s Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed by 2 stat ranks. Then, Deoxys's moves become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Cosmic Power."�\bHis second one, "Attack!", maxes out Deoxys's Special Attack and Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme. Its moves become Psycho Boost, Protect, Zen Headbutt and Cosmic Power."�\bThe third one, "Faster!", maxes out Deoxys's Speed and raises its Evasion by 3 stages and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme. Its moves then become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Double Team."*\bLast but not least, "Defend!" raises the Attack and Special Attack of all Pokémon on Steven's side of the field by 4 stages. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn. Its moves become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Iron Defense."�\bDeoxys's Psycho Boost won't lower its Special Attack, it'll raise it by 2 stages instead. If that wasn't enough, in Attack Forme, there's also a chance for its next physical and special attack to do more damage."�\bAs for Zen Headbutt, while it's in Attack Forme, it'll also have a chance of increasing the user's next physical and special attack, but if it's in any other Forme, it'll instead have an increased chance to flinch."�\bIn Defense Forme, Iron Defense raise the Defense and Special Defense of all Pokémon on its side by 2 stages. For every other move, they are the same move."{\bWally's Trainer Move raises his Gardevoir's Special Attack by 2 stages and Special Defense and Crit Rate by 1 stage."�\bThen, Gardevoir's B Move, B Dazzling Gleam, lower the targets' Attack and Special attack by 4 stages, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks. It can only be used once, but you can't do anything to defend against it."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."3\bApart from that, Kommo-o is pretty standard."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move raises Giratina's Attack and Special Attack by 4 stages and maxes out its Crit Rate. Then, Cynthia can set up a Ghost Zone, which increases the power of Ghost Type attacks."c\bAlso, her Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Special defense of the target by 1 stage."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move raises the Defense and Special Defense of all Pokémon on her side of the field, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll max them out instead."	\bAs for that, her Lucario enters a battle Mega Evolved, while setting up a Fighting Zone. It also has B Aura Sphere, a B Move that can be used after Lucario is attacked twice. After it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of all allies."\bCyrus's Trainer Move raises his Darkrai's Special Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate and Accuracy by 1 stage. In addition, he can set up a Dark Zone to power up Dark type moves, or Darkrai can use Dark Void with 80% accuracy, which in turn then boosts its Dark Pulse."\bDawn's Trainer Move raises the Defense, Special Defense and Crit Rate of all Pokémon on her side of the field, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP. You might be thinking, why, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"�\bCresselia is very tanky, but even more so when it has 50% HP or less. It also is immune to status moves and has Moonlight for healing."@\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move raises the Accuracy and Crit Rate by 2 stages of any Pokémon on her side of the field. In addition, her Rotom has a passive skill which raises its Evasion by 1 stage every time it's hit."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it maxes out its Attack, Crit Rate and Evasion."{\bIn addition, the additional effects of his Sharpedo's moves have a higher chance to occur then it normally it would."�\bHilbert's Trainer Move raises his Genesect's Special Attack by 3 stages, Crit Rate by 2 stages and powers up its next special attack."�\bHis Genesect is able to change form depending on what the target is weakest to, and makes them weaker to that type corresponding form and applies an effect corresponding to its form. As the cherry on top, its Metal Sound hits all opponents."�\bHilda's Trainer Move maxes her Victini's Attack and Crit Rate and when Victini uses V-Create, its stats are raised instead of lowered."�\bN's Trainer Move raises Kyurem's Attack by 4 stages and maxes out its Crit Rate. When Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it halves the damage it takes."�\bIn addition, Kyurem has a B Move. B Noble Roar lowers the Attack, Sp. Atk, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by 2 stat ranks, while it powering up its next physical attack."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"�\bSerena's Trainer Move maxes out her Zygarde's Attack and Special Attack and gives it Gradual Healing. Other than that, Zygarde will be in its Complete Forme the entire battle and can't miss its attacks from Accuracy and Evasion."x\bZygarde's Master Passive also slightly increases the damage it deals and slightly reduces the damage it recieves."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move raises her Marshadow's Attack by 4 stages and Speed and Evasion by 3 stages. Then, in addition with its regular effects, Spectral Thief also boosts 3 of Marshadow's stats by 1 stage."�\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Special Defense by the same amount of stages. Then, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."�\bDiancie's B Move, B Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up. It lowers the opponents' Defense by 2 stages while raising the Defense of itself and its allies by 2 stages."L\bIt also raises Diancie's Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage."~\bLysandre's Trainer Move raises Volcanion's Special Attack by 4 stages, Accuracy by 1 stage and maxes out its Crit Rate."\bThen, B Hydro Pump, which can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned (which Volcanion achieves through a new ability called Scorching Touch). It's an AoE move which deals more damage to burned opponents and makes its next special attack do more damage."@\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana,Acerola,Mina]"�\bLusamine's Trainer Move maxes out Necrozma's Special Attack and lowers its Speed by 1 stage. Necrozma's Prismatic Laser also doesn't require a recharge turn after it's used."�\bIn addition, Necrozma has a Master Passive that increases the damage dealt by its special attacks and reduces the damage it takes from special attacks."f\bHau's Trainer Move raises his Tapu Koko's Special Attack by 4 stages and Crit Rate by 2 stages."�\bTapu Koko extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of the next special attack of itself and its allies when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."\bThen, B Electroweb can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the speed of all targets by 2 stages while raising the speed of Tapu Koko's and its allies by 2 stages."O\bLana's Trainer Move maxes out her Tapu Lele's Attack and Special Attack."�\bTapu Lele extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of its next physical attack and special attack."j\bThen, B Psycho Cut can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move raises the Defense of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 2 stages, maxes out their Crit Rate and if it's sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), their Attack by 2 stages."�\bTapu Bulu extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of the next physical attack of itself and its allies when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."�\bThen, B Swords Dance can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It raises the Attack of Tapu Bulu and its allies by 2 stages and makes their next physical attack do even more damage."\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side of the field and raises the Special Attack of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 4 stages, or maxes it out if it's rainy (which her Tapu Fini can set up). Then they are all granted Gradual Healing."
\bTapu Fini extends the duration of the Fairy Zone it sets up when it enters the battle (because Misty Terrain sucks) and another Passive Skill raises the Defense and Special Defense of itself and its allies by 1 stage when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."+\bThen, B Protect can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It protects itself and its allies from all damage on the turn it's used, then the HP of itself and its allies are restored by 20%, or 30% if Fairy Zone is active and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's rainy."&\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon]"�\bLeon's Trainer Move raises his Eternatus's Special Attack by 3 stages, Crit Rate by 2 stages and lowers its Special Defense by 1 stage. His Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and its Eternabeam doesn't require a recharge turn after it's used."�\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out. Essentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are two types of buffs: Blessings and Immunities."\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat raises at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level. In addition, you can buy a enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assassin's Blessing), for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bImmunites on the other hand, makes your Pokémon immune to status conditions or other effects, like being burned or trapped. All of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."[#SCANNING.......#]"+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"p\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"(\rAwwww, be careful out there. wink"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs<\i>. <i>Sobs<\i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sygna Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out. Essentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are two types of buffs: Blessings and Immunities."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round...".\rsighs I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."d\bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."L\bYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then.">\rDo you know there is a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"S\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you \PN. (The hyphen is important by the way.)"N\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"|\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Nope]"V\bThe Club Challenge, where you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"t\bYou will be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well, you might get some... erhem ...privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"�\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no item, so it's a good place to grind up your Pokemon into top condition!"h\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, a long-lasting battlethon chucking trainers at you until your team drops."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."z\bYour glorious longest run will be logged for you to boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"~\bThe Mayhem Challenge. In this challenge, you are battling with trainers in a full battle, and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's cause they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You will never know what's up their sleeves!"b\bOh, they have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge, you'll fight "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits in the future) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge, you'll be battling Sync Pokemon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"k\bAnyway, want to refresh yourself on a challenge? \ch[1,-1,Club,Practice,Gauntlet,Mayhem,Sygna,Titan]"t\bIn this challenge you can battle characters from the main series games. This is one of the easier challenges."h\bThis challenge is a slightly easier version of the Club Challenge. I'd recommend it for grinding."\\bIn this challenge, trainers are just chucked at you until your team drops. That's it."D\bIn this challenge, you battle trainers with random 6v6 teams."~\bIn this challenge, you'll fight "Sygna Suit" trainers from Pokémon Masters EX in 3v3 triple battles for the most part."�\bIn this challenge, you'll battle Sygna Suit trainers in 6v1 triple battle where the Sygna Suit's ace Pokémon is much tankier."S\bTalk to me again if you'd like to refresh yourself on any of the challenges."\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward."/\b150 GC Credits have been awarded to you."2\b\v[81] GC Credits have been awarded to you.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b30 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same.".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?"9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!"/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day.">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?"*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \V[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL ALTERFICATION OFFER DEAL***,Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits),Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems(1 Credit), Held Items ]"'\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits)]""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Challenge"Win Counts"	Yes?"No![�"s\bMein Kopf tut weh, wenn ich versuche darüber nachzudenken, wie ich diese Herausforderungen meistern soll..."r\bBrauche ich Attacken mit hohem Schaden? Oder sollte ich sie mit Tricks und Statusveränderungen schwächen?"}\bOder vielleicht muss ich die EVs meiner Pokémon anpassen... oder noch schlimmer, nach Pokémon mit hohen IVs jagen..."V\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur DUETT-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?";\bUnd in welchem Schwierigkeitsgrad wirst du antreten?"\bSicher."%\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN!"m\rSieht so aus, als hättest du nicht genug Pokémon zum Kämpfen, was? Ich gebe dir gerade genug, okay?"\r... und fertig! Ta-da!"w\rWas, du hast eine vollständige Heilung erwartet? Haha, sei nicht albern. Das hier ist bereits sehr großzügig."G\rHoffentlich hast du eine gute Zeit bei der Sync-Herausforderung!"2\bWähle deinen Eingang. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]".\bHmph, wenn dies ein Faustkampf wäre..."X\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur TITANEN-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?"�\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Bist du hier, um die Sync-Herausforderung anzunehmen? Ich kann es kaum erwarten, deine Reaktion auf die Trainer hier zu sehen, hehe. ;)"1\bLuc-ker: Du willst ein paar Tipps? Sicher."�\bEs gibt hier ziemlich viele Trainer, also unterteilen wir sie nach ihren Regionen.\n\ch[98,-1,Allgemeine Tipps,Schlüsselbegriffe,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Einall,Kalos,Alola,Galar]"�\bEs gibt hier ziemlich viele Trainer, also unterteilen wir sie nach ihren Regionen.\n\ch[98,-1,Allgemeine Tipps,Schlüsselbegriffe,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Einall,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Sygna-Buffs]")\bViel Glück, du wirst es brauchen."f\bUnd mach dir keine Sorgen, wenn du verlierst, du bekommst trotzdem GK-Credits für den Versuch."�\bDu willst ein paar allgemeine Tipps? Hmm. Der beste Tipp, den ich dir geben kann, ist: Erwarte das Unerwartete. Sie spielen nicht nach der Meta der Hauptspiele, sondern nach der Meta von PoMas."�\bZum Beispiel werden sie ihre Statuswerte viel stärker erhöhen, als sie eigentlich sollten, neue Mechaniken erfinden, Schutzschild ignorieren und sich mehr heilen, als sie sollten, um nur einiges zu nennen."�\bAußerdem zu einigen ihrer „Attacken“: Diese werden nicht vom Pokémon, sondern vom Trainer eingesetzt. Sie können also selbst dann verwendet werden, wenn das Pokémon unter einem Status leidet, der es normalerweise am Bewegen hindern würde."�\bZu guter Letzt funktionieren „Cheese“-Attacken wie Abgangsbund und Abgesang hier nicht; Abschlag wird auch ihre Items nicht entfernen. Versuch es erst gar nicht!";\bWie dem auch sei, viel Glück, du wirst es brauchen."�\bSicher, ich erkläre sie dir.\nVolltrefferquote – wie oft ein Pokémon einen Volltreffer landet, bis maximal 3 Stufen.\nTrainer-Aktion – Eine Aktion, die der Trainer nutzt, um seine Pokémon zu verstärken."V\bS-Attacke – Steht für Synergie-Attacke (Buddy Move). Diese ähneln normalen Attacken, haben aber ein S vor dem Namen. Sie tun meist das, was die normale Attacke tut, aber mit mehr Kraft, Zusatzeffekten oder verstärkten Effekten.\nPassivfähigkeit – Im Grunde eine Fähigkeit. Wie viele ein Pokémon hier hat, ist völlig willkürlich."�\bMaster-Passiv – Eine Passivfähigkeit, die den Schaden des Pokémon erhöht und den erlittenen Schaden verringert.\nZone – Ein Feldeffekt wie Wetter oder Terrain, der Attacken eines bestimmten Typs verstärkt."^\bHeilung pro Runde – Das Pokémon regeneriert in jeder Runde 1/16 seiner maximalen KP."c\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Rocko,Misty,Erika,Giovanni,Rot,Rot (Donnerblitz), Blau,Leaf]"\bRocko hat hier wahrscheinlich das einfachste Set, da er das erste MaMo-Outfit in PoMas ist. Wie auch immer, seine Trainer-Aktion sorgt dafür, dass seine nächste Attacke garantiert trifft und ein Volltreffer wird, aber du kannst dich mit Schutzschild dagegen wehren."�\bVerlass dich auch nicht darauf, dass die Steinkante seines Despotar danebengeht. Sie hat eine bessere Genauigkeit, als man erwarten würde."�\bMisty hat ebenfalls ein sehr einfaches Set. Ihre Trainer-Aktion erhöht die Verteidigung ihres Aquana um 2 Stufen und die Spezial-Verteidigung aller Verbündeten um 2 Stufen."u\bSchließlich hat die Hydropumpe ihres Aquana die Chance, dessen Fluchtwert bei Einsatz um 1 Stufe zu erhöhen."�\bErikas Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Angriff ihres Folipurba um 2 Stufen und die Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe, aber wenn die Sonne scheint, werden diese Werterhöhungen verdoppelt."�\bBei Sonnenschein verdoppelt sich die Initiative ihres Folipurba. Außerdem regeneriert ihr Folipurba am Ende jeder Runde 1/8 seiner maximalen KP."�\bGiovannis Nidoking kann seine Attacken immer zu Volltreffern machen. Sein Megakick ist eine Boden-Attacke, was bedeutet, dass er STAB-Bonus erhält. Zudem kann Nidoking dynamaximieren, und die Dynamax-Attacken werden ebenfalls Volltreffer sein."�\bRot und sein Glurak sind wahnsinnig. Seine Trainer-Aktion erhöht Angriff, Spezial-Angriff und Initiative von Glurak um 3 Stufen und die Volltrefferquote um 2 Stufe, während Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung um 1 Stufe erhöht werden."�\bSein Glurak kann zudem Lohekanonade und Solarstrahl ohne Auflade- oder Erholungsrunde einsetzen, und sie werden niemals ihr Ziel verfehlen."�\bRot hat tatsächlich ein zweites MaMo-Outfit in PoMas. Seine Trainer-Aktion maximiert den Angriff von Pikachu und verleiht ihm kontinuierliche Heilung."�\bPikachu kann auch gigadynamaximieren, obwohl es hier weniger Nutzen daraus zieht als in PoMas, da man einfach eine Dynamax-Attacke pro Sync-Paar raushaut."�\bDarüber hinaus verstärkt Pikachus Master-Passiv „Kanto-Fahnenträger“ seinen Schaden um 10 % und verringert den erlittenen Schaden um 20 %."�\bZu guter Letzt hat Pikachu eine S-Attacke, die genutzt werden kann, wenn ein Elektro-Feld aktiv ist. Wenn dein Pokémon paralysiert ist, werden seine Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung um 1 Stufe gesenkt, sofern es bis dahin nicht besiegt wurde."�\bBlaus Turtok ist der ultimative Tank. Wenn es getroffen wird, erhöht es den Angriff und Spezial-Angriff von sich selbst und seinen Verbündeten um 1 Stufe und heilt sich und seine Verbündeten um 1/16."\bUnd wenn es angreift, werden Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung von ihm selbst und seinen Verbündeten um 1 Stufe erhöht."�\bLeafs Bisaflor hat eine Passivfähigkeit namens „Giftspritze“, die dein Pokémon schwer vergiftet, wenn es von ihm angegriffen wird."�\bZusätzlich dazu senkt der Angriff die Verteidigungswerte deines Pokémon, sodass es in der nächsten Runde noch mehr Schaden erleidet. Schließlich heilt Bisaflor sich nach jedem Angriff um 1/8 seiner Gesundheit – warum auch nicht?"D\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Jens,Klarin,Lyra,Kris,Silber]"�\bJens kann eine Menge. Seine Trainer-Aktion erhöht Verteidigung, Spezial-Verteidigung und Volltrefferquote aller Pokémon auf seiner Seite um 1 Stufe und aktiviert Rückenwind, falls dieser nicht schon aktiv ist."�\bKlarins Trainer-Aktion lässt die nächste Spezial-Attacke seines Lugia viel härter treffen als normal, erhöht seine Genauigkeit um 1 Stufe und maximiert seine Volltrefferquote."�\bAußerdem hat sein Lugia eine Passivfähigkeit, durch die seine Attacken niemals danebengehen, und Klarin hat ein Master-Passiv, das Lugias Spezial-Attacken verstärkt und den Schaden durch gegnerische Spezial-Attacken verringert."�\bLyras Trainer-Aktion erhöht Angriff und Spezial-Angriff aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite um 2 Stufen und verleiht ihnen kontinuierliche Heilung."�\bDas ist aber noch nicht das Verrückteste an diesem Sync-Paar. Das Grasmixer ihres Celebi sorgt dafür, dass das gegnerische Pokémon verwirrt, umklammerrt UND zurückgeschreckt wird. Uuuund sie kann auch ein Grasfeld erzeugen."�\bSchließlich hat Lyra ein Master-Passiv, das Celebis physische Attacken (was nur Grasmixer ist) verstärkt und den erlittenen Schaden durch physische Attacken verringert."4\bWenn du gegen sie antrittst, bete, dass die anderen Sync-Paare physische Angreifer sind, denn sobald es regnet, erhöht ihre Trainer-Aktion den Spezial-Angriff aller Verbündeten um 2 Stufen und die Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe, zudem verursacht die nächste Spezial-Attacke ihrer Verbündeten mehr Schaden."�\bAbgesehen davon macht ihr Suicune nicht viel mehr, obwohl Kris' Master-Passiv dafür sorgt, dass es etwas mehr Schaden verursacht und weniger Schaden durch Angriffe erleidet."�\bSilbers Trainer-Aktion erhöht seinen Angriff und seine Initiative um 3 Stufen und aktiviert Rückenwind auf seiner Seite des Feldes."�\bZudem kann die S-Attacke seines Sniebel, S-Dreifach-Axel, nur genutzt werden, wenn seine KP voll sind. Bei jedem Treffer wird die Initiative des Gegners um 1 Stufe gesenkt, während der eigene Fluchtwert und die Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe steigen."@\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Maike,Bernd,Trojan,Heiko]"�\bMaikes Trainer-Aktion erhöht die Initiative aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite um 2 Stufen, steigert dann den Angriff ihres Lohgock um 4 Stufen sowie die Genauigkeit um 1 Stufe und schützt es für den Rest der Runde vor Schaden."I\bLohgocks Feuerfeger senkt zudem die Verteidigung des Zieles stark."�\bBernds Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff und die Spezial-Verteidigung aller Pokémon auf seiner Seite um 4 Stufen und steigert ihre Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe."'\bWenn sein Latios dann Scheinwerfer einsetzt, wird die Spezial-Verteidigung des Ziels stark gesenkt. Aber glaub nicht, dass ein Unlicht-Typ sicher ist – bei Draco Meteor wird die Volltrefferquote aller Pokémon auf seiner Seite um 1 Stufe erhöht und ihre nächste Spezial-Attacke verstärkt."�\bTrojan... ist eine Hausnummer, sagen wir es mal so. Da er ein Deoxys hat, hat PoMas entschieden, ihm nicht nur eine Form von Deoxys zu geben, sondern alle 4, jede mit einer eigenen Trainer-Aktion."�\bDie erste, „Versuch das mal!“, erzeugt ein Psychofeld und erhöht Verteidigung, Sp.-Angr., Sp.-Vert. und Initiative des Anwenders um 2 Stufen. Danach werden Deoxys' Attacken zu Psycho-Schub, Genesung, Zen-Kopfstoß und Kosmik-Kraft."�\bDie zweite, „Angriff!“, maximiert Deoxys' Spezial-Angriff und Volltrefferquote und lässt Deoxys in die Angriffsform wechseln. Seine Attacken werden zu Psycho-Schub, Schutzschild, Zen-Kopfstoß und Kosmik-Kraft."�\bDie dritte, „Schneller!“, maximiert Deoxys' Initiative, erhöht seinen Fluchtwert um 3 Stufen und lässt Deoxys in die Initiativeform wechseln. Seine Attacken werden dann zu Psycho-Schub, Genesung, Zen-Kopfstoß und Doppelteam."0\bZu guter Letzt: „Verteidigung!“ erhöht den Angriff und Spezial-Angriff aller Pokémon auf Trojans Seite um 4 Stufen. Deoxys wechselt dann in die Verteidigungsform und schützt sich für den Rest der Runde vor Schaden. Seine Attacken werden zu Psycho-Schub, Genesung, Zen-Kopfstoß und Eisenabwehr."�\bDeoxys' Psycho-Schub senkt seinen Spezial-Angriff nicht, sondern erhöht ihn stattdessen um 2 Stufen. Als ob das nicht genug wäre, besteht in der Angriffsform zudem die Chance, dass seine nächste physische und Spezial-Attacke verstärkt werden."�\bWas Zen-Kopfstoß angeht: In der Angriffsform besteht ebenfalls die Chance, den nächsten physischen und Spezial-Angriff des Anwenders zu verstärken; in jeder anderen Form hat er stattdessen eine erhöhte Chance, das Ziel zurückschrecken zu lassen."�\bIn der Verteidigungsform erhöht Eisenabwehr die Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung aller Pokémon auf seiner Seite um 2 Stufen. Alle anderen Attacken bleiben gleich."�\bHeikos Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff seines Guardevoir um 2 Stufen sowie Spezial-Verteidigung und Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe."�\bDanach senkt Guardevoirs S-Attacke, S-Zauberschein, den Angriff und Spezial-Angriff der Ziele um 4 Stufen und macht sie anfälliger für Fee-Attacken. Sie kann nur einmal eingesetzt werden, aber man kann nichts tun, um sich dagegen zu schützen."h\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Antik-Outfit),Cynthia (Aura-Outfit),Zyrus,Lucia]"�\bCynthias Trainer-Aktion, bei der ich mir einige kreative Freiheiten genommen habe, erhöht die Volltrefferquote ihres Grandiras und verstärkt dessen nächste Spezial-Attacke, je nachdem, wie niedrig seine KP sind.">\bAbgesehen davon ist Grandiras ziemlich standardmäßig."�\bDiese Trainer-Aktion von Cynthia erhöht Angriff und Spezial-Angriff von Giratina um 4 Stufen und maximiert seine Volltrefferquote. Dann kann Cynthia eine Phantom-Zone erzeugen, die die Stärke von Geist-Attacken erhöht."o\bZudem senken die Angriffe ihres Giratina die Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung des Ziels um 1 Stufe."�\bDiese Trainer-Aktion von Cynthia erhöht die Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite; ist jedoch eine Kampf-Zone aktiv, werden diese stattdessen maximiert."Q\bIhr Lucario betritt den Kampf direkt in der Mega-Form und erzeugt dabei eine Kampf-Zone. Es verfügt außerdem über S-Aurasphäre, eine S-Attacke, die eingesetzt werden kann, nachdem Lucario zweimal angegriffen wurde. Nachdem sie Schaden verursacht hat, verstärkt sie die nächsten physischen und Spezial-Angriffe aller Verbündeten.":\bZyrus' Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff seines Darkrai um 2 Stufen sowie Volltrefferquote und Genauigkeit um 1 Stufe. Zudem kann er eine Unlicht-Zone erzeugen, um Unlicht-Attacken zu verstärken, oder Darkrai kann Schlummerort mit 80 % Genauigkeit einsetzen, was wiederum seinen Finsteraura verstärkt."3\bLucias Trainer-Aktion erhöht Verteidigung, Spezial-Verteidigung und Volltrefferquote aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite, aber ihr Cresselia erleidet Rückstoßschaden in Höhe von 30 % seiner verbleibenden KP. Du fragst dich vielleicht: Warum, wenn die meisten anderen Trainer-Aktionen keine Nachteile haben?"�\bCresselia ist sehr widerstandsfähig, besonders wenn es 50 % KP oder weniger hat. Zudem ist es immun gegen Status-Attacken und besitzt Mondschein zur Heilung."H\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Kamilla,Anachoret,Warren,Lotta,N]"�\bKamillas Trainer-Aktion erhöht die Genauigkeit und Volltrefferquote aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite um 2 Stufen. Zudem besitzt ihr Rotom eine Passivfähigkeit, die seinen Fluchtwert bei jedem Treffer um 1 Stufe erhöht."�\bAnachorets Trainer-Aktion lässt sein Tohaido Rückstoßschaden in Höhe von 90 % seiner verbleibenden KP erleiden, maximiert dafür aber seinen Angriff, seine Volltrefferquote und seinen Fluchtwert."{\bZudem haben die Zusatzeffekte von Tohaidos Attacken eine höhere Chance einzutreten, als es normalerweise der Fall wäre."�\bWarrens Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff seines Genesect um 3 Stufen, die Volltrefferquote um 2 Stufen und verstärkt seine nächste Spezial-Attacke."�\bSein Genesect kann die Form ändern, je nachdem, wogegen das Ziel am anfälligsten ist, schwächt es gegen diesen Typ und wendet einen zur Form passenden Effekt an. Als Krönung trifft sein Metallsound alle Gegner."�\bLottas Trainer-Aktion maximiert den Angriff und die Volltrefferquote ihres Victini, und wenn Victini V-Generator einsetzt, werden seine Werte erhöht statt gesenkt."�\bNs Trainer-Aktion erhöht Kyurems Angriff um 4 Stufen und maximiert seine Volltrefferquote. Wenn Kyurem sich für Frostvolt auflädt, halbiert es den erlittenen Schaden."�\bZudem besitzt Kyurem eine S-Attacke. S-Abgesang senkt den Angriff, Sp.-Angr. und die Initiative aller gegnerischen Pokémon um 2 Stufen, während es seinen nächsten physischen Angriff verstärkt."F\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Corni,Diantha,Flordelis]"\bSerenas Trainer-Aktion maximiert Angriff und Spezial-Angriff ihres Zygarde und verleiht ihm kontinuierliche Heilung. Ansonsten bleibt Zygarde den gesamten Kampf über in seiner Optimumform und seine Attacken können aufgrund von Genauigkeit oder Fluchtwert nicht danebengehen."y\bZygardes Master-Passiv erhöht zudem leicht den verursachten Schaden und verringert leicht den erlittenen Schaden."�\bCornis Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Angriff ihres Marshadow um 4 Stufen sowie Initiative und Fluchtwert um 3 Stufen. Dann erhöht Diebesschatten, zusätzlich zu den regulären Effekten, 3 von Marshadows Statuswerten um 1 Stufe."
\bWenn die Verteidigung ihres Diancie erhöht wurde, steigert Dianthas Trainer-Aktion dessen Spezial-Verteidigung um die gleiche Anzahl an Stufen. Dann verleiht sie Diancie kontinuierliche Heilung und lässt seine nächste physische Attacke mehr Schaden verursachen."\bDiancies S-Attacke, S-Diamantensturm, kann nur genutzt werden, wenn eine Gesteins-Zone aktiv ist, welche Diantha erzeugen kann. Sie senkt die Verteidigung der Gegner um 2 Stufen, während sie die Verteidigung von sich selbst und seinen Verbündeten um 2 Stufen erhöht."Z\bSie erhöht zudem Diancies Angriff um 2 Stufen und die Volltrefferquote um 1 Stufe."�\bFlordelis' Trainer-Aktion erhöht Volcanions Spezial-Angriff um 4 Stufen, die Genauigkeit um 1 Stufe und maximiert seine Volltrefferquote."=\bDann folgt S-Hydropumpe, die nur genutzt werden kann, wenn mindestens ein gegnerisches Pokémon verbrannt ist (was Volcanion durch eine neue Fähigkeit namens Schmorspitze erreicht). Es ist eine Flächenattacke, die verbrannten Gegnern mehr Schaden zufügt und die nächste Spezial-Attacke des Anwenders verstärkt."E\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Tali,Tracy,Lola,Mati]"�\bLusamines Trainer-Aktion maximiert Necrozmas Spezial-Angriff und senkt seine Initiative um 1 Stufe. Necrozmas Prismather-Laser benötigt zudem keine Erholungsrunde nach dem Einsatz."�\bZusätzlich besitzt Necrozma ein Master-Passiv, das den durch seine Spezial-Attacken verursachten Schaden erhöht und den erlittenen Schaden durch Spezial-Attacken verringert."z\bTalis Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff seines Kapu-Riki um 4 Stufen und die Volltrefferquote um 2 Stufen."
\bKapu-Riki verlängert die Dauer des Elektrofeldes, das es beim Betreten des Kampfes erzeugt, und eine weitere Passivfähigkeit verstärkt die nächste Spezial-Attacke von ihm selbst und seinen Verbündeten, wenn ein neues Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv wird."6\bS-Elektronetz kann dann immer genutzt werden, wenn ein Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv ist. Die Stärke verdoppelt sich in einer Feen-Zone (die Tali erzeugen kann), und es senkt die Initiative aller Ziele um 2 Stufen, während es die Initiative von Kapu-Riki und seinen Verbündeten um 2 Stufen erhöht."S\bTracys Trainer-Aktion maximiert Angriff und Spezial-Angriff ihres Kapu-Fala."�\bKapu-Fala verlängert die Dauer des Psychofeldes, das es beim Betreten des Kampfes erzeugt, und eine weitere Passivfähigkeit verstärkt seinen nächsten physischen und Spezial-Angriff."�\bS-Psychoklinge kann dann immer genutzt werden, wenn ein Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv ist. Sie landet immer einen Volltreffer."�\bLolas Trainer-Aktion erhöht die Verteidigung aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite um 2 Stufen, maximiert ihre Volltrefferquote und, falls die Sonne scheint (was ihr Kapu-Toro bewirken kann), ihren Angriff um 2 Stufen."	\bKapu-Toro verlängert die Dauer des Grasfeldes, das es beim Betreten des Kampfes erzeugt, und eine weitere Passivfähigkeit verstärkt die nächste physische Attacke von ihm selbst und seinen Verbündeten, wenn ein neues Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv wird."�\bS-Schwerttanz kann dann immer genutzt werden, wenn ein Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv ist. Er erhöht den Angriff von Kapu-Toro und seinen Verbündeten um 2 Stufen und lässt ihre nächste physische Attacke noch mehr Schaden verursachen."\bMatis Trainer-Aktion aktiviert Bodyguard auf ihrer Seite des Feldes und erhöht den Spezial-Angriff aller Pokémon auf ihrer Seite um 4 Stufen, oder maximiert ihn sogar, wenn es regnet (was ihr Kapu-Kime bewirken kann). Danach erhalten alle kontinuierliche Heilung."5\bKapu-Kime verlängert die Dauer der Feen-Zone, die es beim Betreten des Kampfes erzeugt (weil Nebelfeld nichts taugt), und eine weitere Passivfähigkeit erhöht Verteidigung und Spezial-Verteidigung von ihm selbst und seinen Verbündeten um 1 Stufe, wenn ein neues Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv wird."i\bS-Schutzschild kann dann immer genutzt werden, wenn ein Wetter, Terrain oder eine Zone aktiv ist. Er schützt es selbst und seine Verbündeten in dieser Runde vor jeglichem Schaden; danach werden 20 % der KP von ihm selbst und seinen Verbündeten regeneriert (bzw. 30 %, wenn eine Feen-Zone aktiv ist), und im Regen werden gesenkte Statuswerte zurückgesetzt.".\bWähle einen Trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Delion]"'\bDelions Trainer-Aktion erhöht den Spezial-Angriff seines Endynalos um 3 Stufen, die Volltrefferquote um 2 Stufen und senkt seine Spezial-Verteidigung um 1 Stufe. Sein Endynalos kann zudem die Unendynamax-Form annehmen, und sein Unendlichstrahl benötigt keine Erholungsrunde nach dem Einsatz."�\bDa ich bemerkt habe, dass der Schwierigkeitsgrad der Sync-Herausforderung ein Fehler war, habe ich dir einige Buffs zur Hilfe gegeben. Im Grunde hast du 7 Energiepunkte für Buffs zur Verfügung. Es gibt zwei Arten von Buffs: Segen und Immunitäten."\bSegen erhöhen die Statuswerte deines Pokémon zu Beginn eines Kampfes und verbrauchen Energie entsprechend ihrer Stufe. Zudem kannst du für ein paar deiner hart erarbeiteten Credits eine verbesserte Version des Buffs kaufen (außer beim Segen des Meuchelmörders)."␀\bImmunitäten hingegen machen dein Pokémon immun gegen Statusveränderungen oder andere Effekte, wie etwa Verbrennungen oder Umklammerung. Alle verbrauchen 2 Energiepunkte und können nicht weiter aufgewertet werden, so wie es bei den Segen möglich ist."N\bIch wünschte, ich könnte an den Fire Ash Discord-Events teilnehmen..."o\bDurch diese Events könnte ich hohe IV-Boosts oder vielleicht seltene Shinies und Legendäre gewinnen..."\bMist..."f\bIch habe vielleicht verloren... Aber meine Entschlossenheit brennt immer noch lichterloh!!!!!!!"e\rSchwester Joy: Es sieht so aus, als müssten deine Pokémon ein wenig zusammengeflickt werden."c\rOh, gut! Deinen Pokémon geht es jetzt wieder prima. Mach dich bereit und pass auf dich auf!"[\rOh, gut! Deinen Pokémon geht es jetzt wieder prima. Viel Glück beim nächsten Mal!"$\bSpielfeldbegrenzung, Kleiner!"<\rDiese Herausforderungen öffnen einem echt die Augen."~\rDieses gewaltige Inferno, dieser erschütternde Eiseshauch. Und als Nächstes kommt ein überwältigender Draco Meteor."_\rWoher kommen diese Trainer nur? Boah... Ich wünschte, ich könnte auch so sein wie sie."9\rConcierge Joi: Willkommen im Secret Grandeur Club!"`\rZahlreiche erstklassige Trainer aus anderen Dimensionen sind für Showdowns eingetroffen!"D\rWähle deine Herausforderung – Belohnungen warten auf dich!"y\rDu kannst mich auch aufsuchen, damit ich dir deine Pokémon zurückgebe, falls du deine Herausforderung verlierst."\rAlles Gute!"A\rWillkommen zurück! Hier sind deine verbliebenen Pokémon."-\rGib nicht auf! Versuch es noch einmal!"8Ansager: Du willst jetzt aufhören? Bist du sicher?"$\bAnsager: Bitte geh nach oben."\bHey \PN."`\bHier wirst du dich mit jemandem deiner Wahl zusammentun, um gegen andere Duos anzutreten."�\bDie Kombinationsmöglichkeiten sind endlos und liegen ganz bei dir. Das bedeutet aber auch, dass du den Sieg nicht vollständig unter Kontrolle hast."\bAufregend, oder?"<\bEin weiterer würdiger Herausforderer kommt und geht."r\bIch sehe deine Begeisterung und deine unerschütterliche Entschlossenheit. Du solltest das Zeug dazu haben."_\bGib nicht auf, junger Mann! Genau wie ich. Ich bin schon seit Ewigkeiten hier. Hohohoho."IBITTE DEIN GC-PAD EINSETZEN, UM AUF DAS JUKEBOX-MENÜ ZUZUGREIFEN..."[#SCANNER LÄUFT.......#]";WILLKOMMEN [\PN]! BITTE WÄHLE DEINE HINTERGRUNDMUSIK."\ch[77,-1,Standard-Beats]"m\ch[77,,Standard-Beats,Frühlings-Violine,Sommer-Flöte,Herbst-Gitarre,Winter-Mundharmonika,Nacht-Piano]"a\rNurse Joi: Das hier ist der Backstage-Bereich, ein Ort, an dem du dich vorbereiten kannst."O\rGönn dir eine Pause. Hol dir einen Kaffee. Geh kurz aufs Klo. Hau rein!"P\rSobald du bereit bist, geh nach oben für deine nächste Herausforderung!"=\rWas für ein Reinfall. Ich habe schon wieder verloren."E\rEs ist wirklich schwer, sie mit nur 3 Pokémon zu bezwingen..."/\rLEHR ES MICH. WIE GEWINNE ICH GEGEN SIE?"\\bHey \PN, du hast den Spießrutenlauf gewählt, was? Über was soll ich also sprechen?"�\bDiese Herausforderung ist simpel. Im Grunde ist es ein Überlebensmodus. Kämpfe gegen deine Herausforderer, bis du fällst. Sei also nicht entmutigt oder traurig, wenn du verlierst. Du hast dein Bestes gegeben."\bAber es unendlich zu machen, fühlt sich nach Sackgasse an, oder? Also habe ich das Limit bei 100 gesetzt. Gut zu wissen, hm?"g\bEin letzter Tipp: Schau ab und zu bei Schwester Joy vorbei, alles klar? Und jetzt los! Abmarsch!"M\bLass mich nachsehen......\nDeine aktuelle Anzahl an Siegen ist \v[81]."\bNoch. Ein. Match.\nZitterst du vor Angst? Bebst du vor Aufregung? Oder wirst du erhobenen Hauptes hier rausmarschieren? Du hast dich jedenfalls toll geschlagen. :) Mach einen Screenshot davon und melde dich bei mir im Discord, du bist des Titels [Gauntlet Maniac] würdig!!!"�\bUrgh... Ich kann dein Gesicht langsam nicht mehr sehen. Nur ein Scherz. Schau dir die Uhrzeit an. Wie lange ist das jetzt her? Hast du schon was gegessen? Gebadet? Du bist bald am Ziel!"�\bHeftig, du bist immer noch hier? Du musst echte Entschlossenheit gezeigt haben, um so lange durchzuhalten. Du solltest diesen Moment per Screenshot festhalten und damit angeben!"�\bDu hast die Halbzeitmarke überschritten! Glückwunsch! Also, wie geht es weiter? Ist hier Endstation für dich? Oder ziehst du diesen scheinbar... endlosen... Kreislauf... weiter durch?"�\bEhrlich, du hast dich gut geschlagen. Das ist eine beachtliche Zahl für engagierte Spieler. Klopf dir selbst auf die Schulter. Ja!"r\bAlles klar, du bist so weit gekommen! Warum stehst du dann hier noch rum? Hmmmm? Hältst du ein Nickerchen?"�\bOkay, das ist ordentlich für Gelegenheitsspieler. Ich möchte dir danken, dass du dich dem Spießrutenlauf gestellt und meine Bemühungen lohnenswert gemacht hast. :)"�\bVielleicht hast du jetzt ein paar Schwierigkeiten. Überleg dir doch, mehr im Training und im Club zu grinden? Hol dir mehr Extras, um deine Pokémon zu verstärken!"g\bHör auf, deine Siege zu zählen, wenn du sie noch an einer Hand abzählen kannst. Ernsthaft. :)"d\bHör auf, deine Siege zu zählen, wenn du dafür nicht mal eine Hand brauchst. Echt jetzt. :)"{\bHey \PN, ich sehe, du hast dich für die Club-Herausforderung entschieden. Lass mich erklären, wie es funktioniert."�\bDie Club-Herausforderung ist eigentlich nur ein kleiner Vorgeschmack auf das, was dich in anderen Teilen des Grandeur Clubs erwartet. Hehehe..."\bAbhängig vom gewählten Schwierigkeitsgrad kämpfst du gegen eine bestimmte Anzahl von Trainern. Als Neuling sind das 3 Arenaleiter, als Veteran 4 Arenaleiter und ein Mitglied der Top Vier, und als Ass sind es 5 Arenaleiter, 2 Mitglieder der Top Vier und ein „Champ“."F\bSprich am Ende mit Hitsu für eine Belohnung für deine Mühen!"k\bHey \PN, ich sehe, du hast dich für die Club-Herausforderung entschieden. Willst du ein paar Tipps?"�\bZunächst einmal solltest du in Erwägung ziehen, Attacken mit etwas niedrigerer Basisstärke, aber mehr AP zu verwenden als die, die du aktuell hast."�\bAuf diese Weise gehen dir mitten im Kampf nicht die AP für eine Attacke aus, was dazu führen könnte, dass du deine Typ-Abdeckung verlierst – und das wäre echt übel."+\bQuelle? Vertrau mir einfach, Kumpel."�\bAls Nächstes solltest du definitiv in Betracht ziehen, deinen Pokémon eine gute Verteilung von Fleißpunkten (FP) zu geben. So lässt du den Gegner nicht mit 1 KP stehen!"�\bVielleicht solltest du auch in Erwägung ziehen, einige Status-Attacken zu nutzen, anstatt dich nur mit roher Gewalt durch einen Kampf zu schlagen."*\bDas ist alles von mir, viel Glück!"(\bBuh. Na ja, trotzdem viel Glück."8Ansager: Du willst jetzt aufhören? Bist du sicher?"^\rNach einer harten Zeit habe ich endlich eine der Club-Herausforderungen geschafft. Puh."�\rBeachte mich gar nicht. Ich grüble nur darüber nach, welche Pokémon ich als Nächstes für meine Herausforderungen mitnehmen soll."X\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur ÜBUNGS-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?"r\bUnd welche Region wirst du herausfordern? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Einall,Kalos, Alola,Kampfzone]"y\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN! Hoffentlich macht dir die Club-Herausforderung keine allzu großen Schwierigkeiten!"y\rEntschuldige, falls du nach einer Heilung suchst. Dieser Service ist in der Club-Herausforderung nicht verfügbar."Z\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN. Deine Pokémon sehen wirklich übel zugerichtet aus."m\rSchwester Joy: Wenn du sie zusammenflicken lassen willst, muss ich dir leider $1.000.000 berechnen. :D"*\rHehe, verzweifelt, was? Alles klar!"H\rJetzt ist alles wieder gut! Mach's gut! Bitte komm bald wieder!!!"i\rHey! Du kannst dir meinen Service nicht leisten! Such das Weite, bevor dir schwarz vor Augen wird!"8\rOoooh, pass da draußen gut auf dich auf. zwinker"b\bHehe, ich werde ständig den Champs zugeteilt! Was für ein Witz von einer Herausforderung."�\b... das würde ich jedenfalls sagen, wenn das nicht ein Traum gewesen wäre, den ich letzte Nacht hatte. Eigentlich bekomme ich nur Arenaleiter zur Auswahl. AHHHHH!"`\b<i>Schluchz<\i>. <i>Schluchz<\i>... Mein Team aus Rattfratz... ausgelöscht. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bDiese Herausforderung hier ist wohl die KOMPLIZIERTESTE HERAUSFORDERUNG im gesamten Grandeur Club. Also hör gut zu. Oder du gehst einfach los und lernst es auf die harte Tour, indem du stolperst und hinfällst."\bDas hier ist im Grunde ein Irrgarten, ein Labyrinth, ein Zuchthaus. Du wählst einen der 6 Eingänge und musst entkommen, indem du 5 Schlüssel sammelst. Die Schlüssel werden an zufällige Trainer verteilt, also musst du sie besiegen, um die Schlüssel zu erhalten."�\bSobald du alle 5 Schlüssel hast, werden alle Eingänge zu Ausgängen, und du musst nur noch den Weg hinaus finden. Alles verstanden? Ich wünsche dir viel Erfolg. :)"�\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Bist du hier, um die Titanen-Herausforderung anzunehmen? Ich kann es kaum erwarten, deine Reaktion auf die Trainer hier zu sehen, hehe. ;)"�\bDa ich bemerkt habe, dass der Schwierigkeitsgrad der MaMo-Herausforderung ein Fehler war, habe ich dir einige Buffs zur Hilfe gegeben. Im Grunde hast du 7 Energiepunkte für Buffs zur Verfügung. Es gibt zwei Arten von Buffs: Segen und Immunitäten."e\bWas ist los, fühlst du dich verloren? Ein Neuling wäre von diesem Ort völlig überwältigt."L\bSuch nach Luc, er wird dir sagen, was dich im Grandeur Club erwartet."b\bWie läuft's? Ich hoffe, du bist nicht überrascht vom Niveau der Trainer im Grandeur Club."�\bSchau ab und zu bei Luc vorbei, um die Regeln und Vorschriften der verschiedenen Herausforderungen zu verstehen. Überdenke bei Bedarf dein Team."`\bWenn du feststeckst, musst du farmen und trainieren. Du wirst es schaffen. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!",\rDiese Herausforderung ist so seltsam."T\rIch weiß nicht, ob ich meinen Partner aufhalte oder ob es andersherum ist...">\rseufz Ich schätze, es hängt alles vom Glück ab, was?"3\bHast du die Herausforderungen abgeschlossen?"B\bIch sehe von Zeit zu Zeit einige Trainer dort herauskommen."9\bIch frage mich, welche Pokémon sie benutzt haben."i\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN! Hoffentlich hast du eine gute Zeit bei der Titanen-Herausforderung!"Z\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN. Deine Pokémon sehen wirklich übel zugerichtet aus."z\bDer Abgrund ist tief und dunkel. Du schauderst, während du spürst, wie überwältigende Kräfte von ihm ausgehen."Z\bDir wurde fast schwarz vor Augen. Es wäre eine gute Idee, sich davon fernzuhalten."]\rNurse Joi: Dies ist der Backstage-Bereich, ein Ort, an dem du dich vorbereiten kannst."P\rSobald du bereit bist, geh nach oben für deine nächste Herausforderung!"S\bBeachte mich gar nicht, ich bereite mich nur mental darauf vor, reinzugehen."Q\bIchwerdediesmalgewinnen, Ichwerdediesmalgewinnen, Ichwerdediesmalgewinnen!"Q\bDies ist ein großartiger Ort, um deine Pokémon auf Level 100 zu bringen!"K\bHitsukid hat diese Herausforderung genau aus diesem Grund entworfen!"�\rIch habe ein Gerücht gehört, dass es früher keine Schwierigkeitsgrade für diese Herausforderung gab und die Trainer sich bei Schwester Joy regelrecht stapelten."^\rErschreckend, oder? Ich bin froh, dass das nicht mehr passiert, falls es jemals so war."
\bAsh"\bSiegfried"\bKamillo"PDas ist ein Getränkeautomat. Ist er wie all die anderen in der Haupthalle?"=BITTE GC-PAD EINSETZEN, UM AUF MAMO-BUFFS ZUZUGREIFEN..."WILLKOMMEN [\PN]!"�DU HAST \v[80] CREDITS AUF DEINEM KONTO. BITTE WÄHLE EINE OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff-Shop,Aktive Buffs ansehen,Freigeschaltete Buffs ansehen,Buff hinzufügen,Aktiven Buff entfernen,Alle aktiven Buffs löschen,Menü schließen]"-DU HAST ALLE VERFÜGBAREN BUFFS GEKAUFT."!DU HAST KEINE AKTIVEN BUFFS."8DU HAST KEINE WEITEREN FREIGESCHALTETEN BUFFS MEHR.""ALLE AKTIVEN BUFFS GELÖSCHT."�Oh weh, es sieht so aus, als hättest du nicht genug kampfbereite Pokémon. Sprich mit Schwester Joy, um sie wieder fit zu machen.",\bPsst! Willst du ein Geheimnis wissen?"�\bIch habe gehört, dass Luc-ker fast wahnsinnig geworden ist, als er versuchte, Trainer aus Passio für diese Herausforderung hierherzuholen."�\bUnd Junge, das hat sich für ihn ausgezahlt. Jetzt haben wir diese Monstrositäten, die als „Herausforderungen“ getarnt sind."V\bDas sind nicht mal „Herausforderungen“, das ist einfach nur reines Mobbing!"�\bIch schätze, der einzige Lichtblick ist die Existenz der Segen... eine Idee, die er bekam, nachdem er viel zu viel von einem Rogue-like-Modus in einem gewissen Spiel gezockt hat."!\bHaha, dein Pech dann wohl."D\rWeißt du, dass es einen Weg in die höheren Stockwerke gibt?"W\rIch habe gehört, dass nur starke Trainer oder bestimmte VIPs Zugang dazu haben."<\rHoffentlich wirst du es dorthin schaffen. Alles Gute!"p\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN! Hoffentlich macht dir die Duett-Herausforderung nicht zu sehr zu schaffen!"t\rEntschuldige, falls du eine Heilung suchst. Dieser Service ist in der Duett-Herausforderung nicht verfügbar."i\rHey! Du kannst dir meinen Service nicht leisten! Such das Weite, bevor dir schwarz vor Augen wird!"/\rHmm... welche Segen sollte ich benutzen?"�\rIch könnte den „Segen des Meuchelmörders“ für zusätzliche Initiative nutzen, damit mein Lucario schnell genug ist, um fast alles zu überholen..."�\bAber ich brauche auch genug Durchschlagskraft, also will ich den „Segen des Kriegers“... oder sollte ich auf ein spezielles Set wechseln und den „Segen des Hexenmeisters“ nutzen, um mein Regieleki noch weiter zu verstärken...?"�\rAh, aber dann kann ich nicht Standfestigkeit bekommen, um mit dem fertigzuwerden, was auch immer <i>das da<\i> ist... ugh. Vielleicht dann einfach Stufe 2 für einen meiner Segen?".\bNur autorisiertes Personal hat Zutritt."�\bFoul: Hallo! Freut mich, dass du endlich hier bist. Falls du mich nicht erkennst: Mein Name ist Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, aber meine Freunde nennen mich einfach Foul."�\bIch bin einer der wenigen Leute, die vor dir ausgewählt wurden, um meine Stärke an diesem Ort zu testen. Und ich kann dir aus Erfahrung sagen, dass du hier eine Menge Spaß haben wirst – oder auch nicht. Es hängt schließlich ganz von dir ab."|\bMan sieht Unmengen riesiger Experimentierbehälter mit schwebenden Exemplaren in farbenfrohen, sprudelnden Flüssigkeiten."S\bMann, ich liebe diese Herausforderung, auch wenn sie so verdammt schwer ist."�\bDie verschiedenen Trainer, gegen die man antritt, ihre einzigartigen Kniffe, ihr Style und sogar die Segen, die man benutzen kann."\bEs ist wunderschön. :')"U\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur CLUB-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?"W\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur MAYHEM-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?"�\bFür diesen Durchlauf behältst du zwar deinen Beutel, hast aber nur eine festgelegte Anzahl an Items zur Verfügung. Keine Sorge, du bekommst deinen Beutel früh genug zurück."1\bMan sieht faszinierende farbige Exemplare."O\bSpielfeldbegrenzu...... hmmmm? Lass mich mal kurz diesen Anruf annehmen."0\bJa, Sir? Ja. Ja. Er ist hier. Verstanden."b\bEntschuldigung. Du darfst eintreten und ab sofort das obere Stockwerk betreten. Bitte sehr."7\bHoffentlich hast du Spaß im Grandeur Club, \PN!"G\bMöchtest du dein Wissen über eine Herausforderung auffrischen?"j\bYo! Ich bin Luc-ker, freut mich, dich kennenzulernen, \PN. (Der Bindestrich ist übrigens wichtig.)"_\bHmm? Woher ich deinen Namen kenne? Ahahaha, mach dir über die Details mal keine Sorgen."\bWie dem auch sei, ich bin hier, um dir ein paar Infos zu den Herausforderungen zu geben, so wie Hitsu es von mir wollte."q\bDu solltest sie dir besser auf einem Zettel notieren, anstatt einfach nur dauernd Bestätigen zu drücken!"a\bEs gibt 6 Hauptherausforderungen im Grandeur Club. Über welche möchtest du etwas wissen?"�\ch[1,-1,Club-Herausforderung,Übungs-Herausforderung,Gauntlet-Herausforderung,Mayhem-Herausforderung,Sync-Herausforderung,Titanen-Herausforderung,Nö]"b\bDie Club-Herausforderung, bei der du gegen Charaktere aus den Hauptspielen kämpfen kannst."�\bWenn man gegen Charaktere aus dem Anime und Pokémon Adventures kämpfen kann, warum dann nicht auch gegen die aus den Hauptspielen?"�\bDu wirst gegen Pokémon auf Level 90 in einem 3-gegen-3-Kampf antreten. Wenn du dich gut schlägst, erhältst du vielleicht ein paar... hüstel ...Privilegien.",\bMöchtest du sonst noch etwas wissen?"n\bDie Übungs-Herausforderung. Wenn die Club-Herausforderung zu schwer für dich ist, versuch es hiermit!"�\bÄhnlich wie die Club-Herausforderung, aber die Pokémon sind auf Level 75 und tragen keine Items – also ein guter Ort, um deine Pokémon in Topform zu bringen!"�\bDie Gauntlet-Herausforderung, ein Marathon-Kampf, bei dem dir so lange Trainer entgegengeworfen werden, bis dein Team am Ende ist."�\bDu kämpfst gegen Pokémon auf Level 100 in 3-gegen-3-Kämpfen, wobei du in bestimmten Intervallen Vorteile erhältst, die dir helfen, deine Siegesserie auszubauen."�\bDein glorreichster Rekordversuch wird gespeichert, damit du im Discord vor anderen Spielern damit prahlen kannst – also fahr die schweren Geschütze auf!"�\bDie Mayhem-Herausforderung. In dieser Herausforderung trittst du gegen Trainer in einem vollen Kampf an, und alle ihre Pokémon sind auf Level 100."�\bWenn du aufpasst, wirst du merken, dass selbst wenn du beim nächsten Mal auf denselben Trainer triffst, seine Teamaufstellung fast nie dieselbe ist!"�\bDas liegt daran, dass sie einen Pool an Pokémon haben, die nur auf dich warten. Du wirst nie wissen, was sie als Nächstes aus dem Hut zaubern!"u\bOh, und sie haben auch hohe IVs, also bring besser deine 6 Besten mit, denn DAS HIER IST DER REINSTE WAHNSINN!"�\bDie Sync-Herausforderung: Hier kämpfst du gegen Trainer in „MaMo-Outfits“ (und künftig auch anderen Outfits) aus dem Mobile-Hit „Pokémon Masters EX“ in 3-gegen-3-Dreierkämpfen."�\bIhre Pokémon können auch spezielle Kniffe beherrschen, zum Beispiel keine Erholungsrunde nach einer Attacke mit hoher Basisstärke zu benötigen oder niemals ihr Ziel zu verfehlen."S\bBring besser deinen Glücksbringer mit, diese Herausforderung ist knallhart!"�\bDie Titanen-Herausforderung: Du kämpfst gegen Sync-Pokémon, auch bekannt als Titanen, in einem 6-gegen-1-Dreierkampf. <s>Das wurde vor Karmesin und Purpur entwickelt, lange bevor die dachten, das sei cool.</s>"�\bSie behalten ihre Kniffe aus der Sync-Herausforderung bei, sind aber viel zäher, und du kannst dich nicht auf Flächenattacken verlassen."�\bHitsus Idee dahinter ist, das Szenario von Quest-Raids aus gewissen RPGs nachzuahmen. Also mach dich bereit und ziel auf den Kopf!"2\bPuh! Danke dafür. Viel Glück da draußen!"�\bWie dem auch sei, willst du dein Wissen über eine Herausforderung auffrischen? \ch[1,-1,Club,Übung,Gauntlet,Mayhem,Sygna,Titan]"�\bIn dieser Herausforderung kannst du gegen Charaktere aus den Hauptspielen kämpfen. Das ist eine der leichteren Herausforderungen."x\bDiese Herausforderung ist eine etwas leichtere Version der Club-Herausforderung. Ich empfehle sie zum Trainieren."{\bIn dieser Herausforderung werden dir einfach so lange Trainer entgegengeworfen, bis dein Team am Ende ist. Das ist alles."[\bIn dieser Herausforderung kämpfst du gegen Trainer mit zufälligen 6-gegen-6-Teams."�\bIn dieser Herausforderung kämpfst du zum Großteil gegen Trainer in „MaMo-Outfits“ aus Pokémon Masters EX in 3-gegen-3-Dreierkämpfen."�\bIn dieser Herausforderung kämpfst du gegen MaMo-Trainer in einem 6-gegen-1-Dreierkampf, wobei das Signatur-Pokémon des Trainers viel widerstandsfähiger ist."i\bSprich mich wieder an, wenn du dein Wissen über eine der Herausforderungen auffrischen möchtest."\bWas zur Hölle."�\bIch habe mein Necrozma zum Super-Spezialtraining gebracht, um seine IVs zu maximieren. Es hat 252 EVs auf Spezial-Angriff. Es ist mäßig."}\bWARUM ZUR HÖLLE MACHT SEINE Z-ATTACKE NACH DER ULTRA-METAMORPHOSE DANN NUR 30 BIS 35 % SCHADEN BEI MISTYS POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bZeig mir dein Bestes!"N\bRocko: Die Welt ist riesig. Es gibt noch viele starke Trainer wie dich."@\bIch habe vollstes Vertrauen, dass du sie bezwingen wirst!"U\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN. Dein Team sieht wirklich übel zugerichtet aus."�\rDie Maschine hinter mir ist kaputtgegangen, also gibt es für den Rest der Herausforderung keine Heilung mehr für dich, ob du willst oder nicht."&\rKomm beim nächsten Mal wieder!"B\rDie Maschine ist voll aufgeladen. Heilen wir dein Team, ja?"9\rJetzt ist alles wieder gut! Gib dein Bestes, okay?"s\rHehe, verzweifelt, was? Ich könnte dich mit der Maschine hinter mir heilen, aber sie ist noch nicht bereit."\rHeftig."�\rEntweder haben diese Titanen eine lachhafte Menge an KP und/oder Verteidigung, oder unser Schaden wird um einen wahnsinnigen Betrag reduziert."b\rTja. So oder so fühlt es sich jedes Mal an, als würde man gegen einen JRPG-Boss kämpfen."D\bGlückwunsch, du hast die ÜBUNGS-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"L\bAbhängig vom gewählten Schwierigkeitsgrad ist hier deine Belohnung.",\bDir wurde 1 GC-Credit gutgeschrieben."3\bTritt ruhig wieder an für mehr Belohnungen!"�\bDu kannst den Ausgang finden, indem du dem Pfeil folgst; es ist besser, sich hier nicht unnötig lange aufzuhalten. Alles klar?"b\bNein, nein, nein. Keine Belohnungen mehr. Aber du kannst es jederzeit wieder versuchen, ja?"A\bGlückwunsch, du hast die CLUB-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!".\bDir wurden 2 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben.".\bDir wurden 5 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben.".\bDir wurden 3 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."/\bDir wurden 10 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."E\bGlückwunsch, du hast die GAUNTLET-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"?\bAbhängig von deinem Durchlauf ist hier deine Belohnung."0\bDir wurden 150 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."3\bDir wurden \v[81] GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."C\bGlückwunsch, du hast die MAYHEM-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"/\bDir wurden 30 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."/\bDir wurden 50 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."/\bDir wurden 75 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."B\bGlückwunsch, du hast die DUETT-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"/\bDir wurden 15 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."/\bDir wurden 25 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."A\bGlückwunsch, du hast die SYNC-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"/\bDir wurden 20 GC-Credits gutgeschrieben."D\bGlückwunsch, du hast die TITANEN-HERAUSFORDERUNG gemeistert!"e\rHeh. Egal wie oft du diese Herausforderung machst, es gibt keine zwei identischen Durchläufe."p\rNa ja, okay. Vielleicht doch, aber die Chance liegt bei etwa 0,000000000000000000000000000000000000001 %."�\bIm Ernst jetzt. Es gibt so viele Trainer und ihre Teams sind vielleicht nicht mal jedes Mal dieselben, selbst wenn du auf denselben Trainer triffst."�\rUND es ist vielleicht nicht mal dieselbe Reihenfolge oder dieselben Räume wie beim letzten Mal, selbst wenn die Trainer dieselben sind.":\bWie läuft's? Wetten, du schlägst dich großartig!"Q\bDu wirst das meistern und deinen Weg hierher zurückfinden. Hab ich recht?"E\bAh, die Herausforderungen hier sind viel härter als erwartet."%\bDas deprimiert mich ein wenig."%\bUnd du? Bist du bereit dafür?"=\rWow, das ist köstlich! Bitte noch eins zum Mitnehmen!"N\bHmm. Es ist so schwer, für jeden Trainer eine Strategie zu entwickeln."�\bDie Sache ist die, es gibt keine „perfekte Eröffnung“. Du könntest mit einem Tentantel anfangen und es wäre fantastisch gegen Benson, aber dann würde es von jedem von Ignaz’ Pokémon mit einem Schlag besiegt werden."~\bUnd dann müsstest du Items verschwenden... oder noch schlimmer, du hättest ein Pokémon weniger für den Rest der Kämpfe."z\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN! Hoffentlich nutzt du diese Gelegenheit, um deine Pokémon auf Vordermann zu bringen!"Q\r..........hoffentlich bist du nicht für eine schnelle Heilung hier, oder?"e\rWow... Ähm, dieser Service ist in der Übungs-Herausforderung nicht verfügbar. Tut mir leid."%\rGib dein Bestes... alles klar?";\rSchwester Joy: Großartig! Hol dir diese Siege, \PN!"A\bDas ist unmenschlich. Ich mach für heute wohl Feierabend."I\bDieses Currygericht ist genau wie meine Herausforderungen im Club."(\bEs macht mich fertig... Schluchz."m\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur GAUNTLET-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Deine höchste Siegesserie liegt bei \v[93]."\bMöchtest du teilnehmen?"(\bIch wurde letzten Monat gefeuert."�\bJetzt habe ich nichts Besseres zu tun, als das hier zu suchten. Meine längste Siegesserie liegt bei 70... Heilungen werden immer seltener, je weiter man kommt."~\bHey \PN, ich sehe, du hast dich für die Übungs-Herausforderung entschieden. Lass mich erklären, wie es funktioniert."�\bDie Übungs-Herausforderung ist im Grunde eine leichtere Version der Club-Herausforderung, damit du deine Pokémon zur Vorbereitung darauf trainieren kannst. Mit anderen Worten: Wir haben diese Herausforderung zum Grinden entworfen."n\bHey \PN, ich sehe, du hast dich für die Übungs-Herausforderung entschieden. Willst du ein paar Tipps?"FBITTE GC-PAD EINSETZEN, UM AUF DAS BELOHNUNGSMENÜ ZUZUGREIFEN..."jWILLKOMMEN [\PN]! DU HAST \V[80] CREDITS AUF DEINEM KONTO. BITTE WÄHLE EINE BELOHNUNG ZUM EINLÖSEN."�\ch[98,-1,***SPEZIELLES MUTATIONS-ANGEBOT***,Verbesserungen (1 Credit),Mutation (3 Credits),Lounge-Musik-Paket (10 Credits),Edelsteine (1 Credit),Getragene Items ]")\ch[75,-1, Code: Glück (2 Credits)]")EINLÖSUNG ERFOLGREICH! VIELEN DANK!")BITTE ENTNIMM DEIN PAD! VIELEN DANK!"ADU HAST NICHT GENUG CREDITS. BITTE KOMM EIN ANDERMAL WIEDER."p\ch[75,-1,Intensitäts-Tonikum, Vital-Serum, Dichtes Extrakt,Verborgenes Stimulans,Apex-Vakzin,Blitz-Bräu]"V\ch[75,-1,Code: Atem,Code: Grimm,Code: Wall,Code: Sturm,Code: Kuppel,Code: Glanz]"aLOUNGE-MUSIK-PAKET BEREITS GEKAUFT UND HERUNTERGELADEN! BITTE ENTNIMM DEIN PAD! VIELEN DANK!"JLOUNGE-MUSIK-PAKET AUF DAS GRANDEUR-PAD HERUNTERGELADEN! VIELEN DANK!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]">\bBwahahahaha. Ich... mich schaudert es auf dieser Etage."IBITTE GC-PAD EINSETZEN, UM AUF DEINE GRANDEUR-REKORDE ZUZUGREIFEN..."@WELCHE REKORDE MÖCHTEST DU PRÜFEN? \ch[98,-1,Übung,Club]"%Deine Übungs-Rekorde sind leer.""Deine Club-Rekorde sind leer."VWELCHE REKORDE MÖCHTEST DU PRÜFEN? \ch[98,-1,Übung,Club,Gauntlet,Duett,Mayhem]"&Deine Gauntlet-Rekorde sind leer."#Deine Duett-Rekorde sind leer."$Deine Mayhem-Rekorde sind leer."]\bBitte störe mich nicht. Ich muss eine Strategie für die Herausforderungen entwerfen."d\bEntschuldigung, du brauchst mindestens 3 kampfbereite Pokémon für die Sync-Herausforderung."U\bHallo, dies ist der Eingang zur SYNC-HERAUSFORDERUNG. Möchtest du teilnehmen?"e\rIch habe gehört, dass noch viel mehr Herausforderer aus der ganzen Welt hierhergekommen sind."M\rDadurch werde ich erfahren, wo ich auf meinem Weg an die Spitze stehe!"h\rSchwester Joy: Guten Tag, \PN! Hoffentlich hast du eine gute Zeit bei der Mayhem-Herausforderung!"m\rSchwester Joy: Wenn du sie zusammenflicken lassen willst, muss ich dir leider $1.000.000 berechnen. :D"Ja"	Nein"Neuling"Veteran"Ass"Herausforderung"Anzahl der Siege"Ja?"
Nein!;[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!"[\rLooks like you don't have enough 'mons to battle huh? I'll give you just enough, OK?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\n\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\n\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn, Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Sygna Buffs]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."K\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bAlso, about some of their "moves". They're not used by the Pokémon, they're used by the trainer, so they can be used even when the Pokémon's been afflicted with a condition that would normally stop them from moving."�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure, I'll explain them.\nCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages.\nTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses, which provide buffs to their Pokémon."H\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. These are similar to regular moves, except they have a B in front of the move's name. They usually do what the regular move does, with increased power or added effects or the regular effect enhanced.\nPassive Skill - Essentially an ability. How many a Pokémon has here is completely arbitrary."�\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the Pokémon's damage and reduces the damage it takes.\nZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type."Q\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn."]\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika,Giovanni,Red,Red (Thunderbolt), Blue,Leaf]"�\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit. Anyway, his Trainer Move makes his next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but you can protect against it."i\bAlso, don't count on his Tyranitar's Stone Edge to miss. It has better accuracy than you'd expect."�\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move raises her Vaporeon's Defense by 2 stages and all allies' Special Defense by 2 stages."e\bLastly, her Vaporeon's Hydro Pump has a chance to raise its Evasion by 1 stage when it's used."�\bErika's Trainer Move raises her Leafeon's Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage, but if the Sun's up, these stat raises are doubled."\bWith the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled. Lastly, her Leafeon will restore 1/8th of its max HP at the every turn."�\bGiovanni's Nidoking is able to always make its attacks critical hits. Its Mega Kick is a Ground type attack, meaning it gains STAB from it. In addition, Nidoking can also Dynamax and the Max Moves will be critical hits too."�\bRed and his Charizard are insane. His Trainer Move raises Charizard's Attack, Special Attack and Speed by 3 stages and Crit Rate by 2 stages, though its Defense and Special Defense is increased by 1 stage."�\bHis Charizard is also able to use Blast Burn and Solar Beam without needing a (re)charging turn and they will also never miss."\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move maxes out Pikachu's Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since you just throw out 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair."}\bFuthermore, Pikachu's Master Passive, Kanto Flag Bearer, boosts its damage by 10% and reduces its damage taken by 20%."�\bLastly, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a Buddy Move which can be used when Electric Terrain's active. If your Pokémon's paralysed, its Defense and Special Defense are lowered by 1 stage, if they haven't fainted by that point."�\bBlue's Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, it raises the Attack and Special Attack of itself and its allies by 1 stage and heals 1/16th of itself and its allies."p\bAnd then when it attacks, the Defense and Special Defense of itself and its allies are raised by 1 stage."}\bLeaf's Venusaur has a passive skill called Venomous, which badly poisons your Pokémon if your Pokémon is atttacked by it."�\bIn addition to that, the attack will lower the defensive stats of your pokemon, so your pokemon will take even more damage on the next turn. Lastly, Venusaur will heal itself for 1/8th of its health after every attack, because why not?">\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris,Silver]"�\bMorty does a lot. His Trainer Move increases the Defense, Special Defense and Crit Rate of all Pokémon on his side of the field by 1 stage and sets up Tailwind if it isn't already active."�\bEthan's Trainer Move makes the next special attack his Lugia use hit a lot harder than it would, as well as increasing its Accuracy by 1 stage and maxing out its Crit Rate."�\bAlso, his Lugia has a Passive Skill which makes its attacks never miss and Ethan has a Master Passive which boosts its special attacks and reduces damage it takes from opposing special attacks."�\bLyra's Trainer Move increases the Attack and Special Attack of any Pokémon on her side by 2 stages and gives them Gradual Healing."�\bThat's not the crazy thing about this sync pair though. Her Celebi's Grassy Glide makes the opposing Pokémon become confused, trapped AND flinched. Annnnd she can set up Grassy Terrain too."�\bLastly, Lyra has a Master Passive which boosts Celebi's physical attacks (which is just Grassy Glide) as well as reducing the damage it takes from physical attacks."�\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers, because once the Rain is up, her Trainer Move raises all allies' Special Atttack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage, as well as her allies' next special attack doing more damage."�\bApart from that, her Suicune doesn't do much else, though Kris's Master Passive makes it deal a little more damage and reduces the damage it takes from attacks."v\bSilver's Trainer Move increases its Attack and Speed by 3 stages and sets up Tailwind on his side of the field."�\bIn addition, his Sneasel's B Move, B Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. On every hit, the opposing Pokémon's Speed is lowered by 1 stage while its own Evasion and Crit Rate are increased by 1 stage.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move increases the speed of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 2 stages, then increases her Blaziken's Attack by 4 stages and Accuracy by 1 stage and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."K\bBlaziken's Blaze Kick also sharply lowers the Defense of its target."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move increases the Special Attack and Special Defense of all Pokémon on his side of the field by 4 stages as well as increasing their Crit Rate by 1 stage."4\bThen, when his Latios uses Luster Purge, the Special Defense of the target is sharply lowered. But don't think bringing in a Dark type is safe either - when using Draco Meteor his all Pokémon on its side have their Crit Rate increased by 1 stage as well as having their next special attack do more damage."�\bSteven... is a lot, let's just say. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4 forms, each with a Trainer Move."�\bHis first one, "Try This!", sets up Psychic Terrain and raises the user’s Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed by 2 stat ranks. Then, Deoxys's moves become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Cosmic Power."�\bHis second one, "Attack!", maxes out Deoxys's Special Attack and Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme. Its moves become Psycho Boost, Protect, Zen Headbutt and Cosmic Power."�\bThe third one, "Faster!", maxes out Deoxys's Speed and raises its Evasion by 3 stages and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme. Its moves then become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Double Team."*\bLast but not least, "Defend!" raises the Attack and Special Attack of all Pokémon on Steven's side of the field by 4 stages. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn. Its moves become Psycho Boost, Recover, Zen Headbutt and Iron Defense."�\bDeoxys's Psycho Boost won't lower its Special Attack, it'll raise it by 2 stages instead. If that wasn't enough, in Attack Forme, there's also a chance for its next physical and special attack to do more damage."�\bAs for Zen Headbutt, while it's in Attack Forme, it'll also have a chance of increasing the user's next physical and special attack, but if it's in any other Forme, it'll instead have an increased chance to flinch."�\bIn Defense Forme, Iron Defense raise the Defense and Special Defense of all Pokémon on its side by 2 stages. For every other move, they are the same move."{\bWally's Trainer Move raises his Gardevoir's Special Attack by 2 stages and Special Defense and Crit Rate by 1 stage."�\bThen, Gardevoir's B Move, B Dazzling Gleam, lower the targets' Attack and Special attack by 4 stages, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks. It can only be used once, but you can't do anything to defend against it."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."3\bApart from that, Kommo-o is pretty standard."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move raises Giratina's Attack and Special Attack by 4 stages and maxes out its Crit Rate. Then, Cynthia can set up a Ghost Zone, which increases the power of Ghost Type attacks."c\bAlso, her Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Special defense of the target by 1 stage."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move raises the Defense and Special Defense of all Pokémon on her side of the field, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll max them out instead."	\bAs for that, her Lucario enters a battle Mega Evolved, while setting up a Fighting Zone. It also has B Aura Sphere, a B Move that can be used after Lucario is attacked twice. After it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of all allies."\bCyrus's Trainer Move raises his Darkrai's Special Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate and Accuracy by 1 stage. In addition, he can set up a Dark Zone to power up Dark type moves, or Darkrai can use Dark Void with 80% accuracy, which in turn then boosts its Dark Pulse."\bDawn's Trainer Move raises the Defense, Special Defense and Crit Rate of all Pokémon on her side of the field, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP. You might be thinking, why, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"�\bCresselia is very tanky, but even more so when it has 50% HP or less. It also is immune to status moves and has Moonlight for healing."@\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move raises the Accuracy and Crit Rate by 2 stages of any Pokémon on her side of the field. In addition, her Rotom has a passive skill which raises its Evasion by 1 stage every time it's hit."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it maxes out its Attack, Crit Rate and Evasion."{\bIn addition, the additional effects of his Sharpedo's moves have a higher chance to occur then it normally it would."�\bHilbert's Trainer Move raises his Genesect's Special Attack by 3 stages, Crit Rate by 2 stages and powers up its next special attack."�\bHis Genesect is able to change form depending on what the target is weakest to, and makes them weaker to that type corresponding form and applies an effect corresponding to its form. As the cherry on top, its Metal Sound hits all opponents."�\bHilda's Trainer Move maxes her Victini's Attack and Crit Rate and when Victini uses V-Create, its stats are raised instead of lowered."�\bN's Trainer Move raises Kyurem's Attack by 4 stages and maxes out its Crit Rate. When Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it halves the damage it takes."�\bIn addition, Kyurem has a B Move. B Noble Roar lowers the Attack, Sp. Atk, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by 2 stat ranks, while it powering up its next physical attack."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"�\bSerena's Trainer Move maxes out her Zygarde's Attack and Special Attack and gives it Gradual Healing. Other than that, Zygarde will be in its Complete Forme the entire battle and can't miss its attacks from Accuracy and Evasion."x\bZygarde's Master Passive also slightly increases the damage it deals and slightly reduces the damage it recieves."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move raises her Marshadow's Attack by 4 stages and Speed and Evasion by 3 stages. Then, in addition with its regular effects, Spectral Thief also boosts 3 of Marshadow's stats by 1 stage."�\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Special Defense by the same amount of stages. Then, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."�\bDiancie's B Move, B Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up. It lowers the opponents' Defense by 2 stages while raising the Defense of itself and its allies by 2 stages."L\bIt also raises Diancie's Attack by 2 stages and Crit Rate by 1 stage."~\bLysandre's Trainer Move raises Volcanion's Special Attack by 4 stages, Accuracy by 1 stage and maxes out its Crit Rate."\bThen, B Hydro Pump, which can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned (which Volcanion achieves through a new ability called Scorching Touch). It's an AoE move which deals more damage to burned opponents and makes its next special attack do more damage."@\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana,Acerola,Mina]"�\bLusamine's Trainer Move maxes out Necrozma's Special Attack and lowers its Speed by 1 stage. Necrozma's Prismatic Laser also doesn't require a recharge turn after it's used."�\bIn addition, Necrozma has a Master Passive that increases the damage dealt by its special attacks and reduces the damage it takes from special attacks."f\bHau's Trainer Move raises his Tapu Koko's Special Attack by 4 stages and Crit Rate by 2 stages."�\bTapu Koko extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of the next special attack of itself and its allies when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."\bThen, B Electroweb can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the speed of all targets by 2 stages while raising the speed of Tapu Koko's and its allies by 2 stages."O\bLana's Trainer Move maxes out her Tapu Lele's Attack and Special Attack."�\bTapu Lele extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of its next physical attack and special attack."j\bThen, B Psycho Cut can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move raises the Defense of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 2 stages, maxes out their Crit Rate and if it's sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), their Attack by 2 stages."�\bTapu Bulu extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets up when it enters the battle and another Passive Skill boosts the damage of the next physical attack of itself and its allies when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."�\bThen, B Swords Dance can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It raises the Attack of Tapu Bulu and its allies by 2 stages and makes their next physical attack do even more damage."\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side of the field and raises the Special Attack of all Pokémon on her side of the field by 4 stages, or maxes it out if it's rainy (which her Tapu Fini can set up). Then they are all granted Gradual Healing."
\bTapu Fini extends the duration of the Fairy Zone it sets up when it enters the battle (because Misty Terrain sucks) and another Passive Skill raises the Defense and Special Defense of itself and its allies by 1 stage when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."+\bThen, B Protect can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It protects itself and its allies from all damage on the turn it's used, then the HP of itself and its allies are restored by 20%, or 30% if Fairy Zone is active and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's rainy."&\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon]"�\bLeon's Trainer Move raises his Eternatus's Special Attack by 3 stages, Crit Rate by 2 stages and lowers its Special Defense by 1 stage. His Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and its Eternabeam doesn't require a recharge turn after it's used."�\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out. Essentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are two types of buffs: Blessings and Immunities."\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat raises at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level. In addition, you can buy a enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assassin's Blessing), for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bImmunites on the other hand, makes your Pokémon immune to status conditions or other effects, like being burned or trapped. All of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."[#SCANNING.......#]"+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"p\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"(\rAwwww, be careful out there. wink"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs<\i>. <i>Sobs<\i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sygna Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out. Essentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are two types of buffs: Blessings and Immunities."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round...".\rsighs I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."d\bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."L\bYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then.">\rDo you know there is a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"S\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you \PN. (The hyphen is important by the way.)"N\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"|\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Nope]"V\bThe Club Challenge, where you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"t\bYou will be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well, you might get some... erhem ...privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"�\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no item, so it's a good place to grind up your Pokemon into top condition!"h\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, a long-lasting battlethon chucking trainers at you until your team drops."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."z\bYour glorious longest run will be logged for you to boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"~\bThe Mayhem Challenge. In this challenge, you are battling with trainers in a full battle, and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's cause they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You will never know what's up their sleeves!"b\bOh, they have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge, you'll fight "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits in the future) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge, you'll be battling Sync Pokemon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"k\bAnyway, want to refresh yourself on a challenge? \ch[1,-1,Club,Practice,Gauntlet,Mayhem,Sygna,Titan]"t\bIn this challenge you can battle characters from the main series games. This is one of the easier challenges."h\bThis challenge is a slightly easier version of the Club Challenge. I'd recommend it for grinding."\\bIn this challenge, trainers are just chucked at you until your team drops. That's it."D\bIn this challenge, you battle trainers with random 6v6 teams."~\bIn this challenge, you'll fight "Sygna Suit" trainers from Pokémon Masters EX in 3v3 triple battles for the most part."�\bIn this challenge, you'll battle Sygna Suit trainers in 6v1 triple battle where the Sygna Suit's ace Pokémon is much tankier."S\bTalk to me again if you'd like to refresh yourself on any of the challenges."\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward."/\b150 GC Credits have been awarded to you."2\b\v[81] GC Credits have been awarded to you.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b30 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same.".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?"9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!"/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day.">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?"*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \V[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL ALTERFICATION OFFER DEAL***,Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits),Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems(1 Credit), Held Items ]"'\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits)]""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Challenge"Win Counts"	Yes?"No!Iu;␀[[%"2\bThis might help you beat the P1 Grand Prix."&\bUse it well and win that thing.")\bThis is my trusted pal, Poliwrath."=\bIt evolved from a Poliwhirl when I used a Water Stone."-Celadon City Pokémon Gym Leader:\nErika" The Nature-Loving Princess!"C\rI got my Koffing in Cinnabar. It breathes poison when angry."!\bGary: How's it going, \PN?"J\bWhat? You only have four badges? What a loser! I already have five.")\bAnd how many Pokémon do you have?"_\bThat's not nearly as many as me! You'll never catch up to the legendary Gary Oak. Later!"3Find what you need at the Celadon Dept. Store!"\rPoli"&My boyfriend taught me this mov